  "nl_text": "The database name is rschema_0133, and it contains five tables. The first table, Book_Category, has three columns: Book_Type_ID, Description, and Type_Name. Book_Type_ID is the primary key, and Description and Type_Name are both strings. The second table, Reader_Category, has three columns: Description, Reader_Type_ID, and Type_Name. Reader_Type_ID is the primary key, and Description and Type_Name are both strings. The third table, Book, has nine columns: Author, Book_ID, Book_Type_ID, Content_Description, Price, Publication_Date, Publisher, Title, and a foreign key to Book_Category. Book_ID is the primary key, and Book_Type_ID is a foreign key to Book_Category. The fourth table, Reader, has six columns: Contact_Number, Credit_Score, Description, Reader_ID, Reader_Type_ID, and a foreign key to Reader_Category. Reader_ID is the primary key, and Reader_Type_ID is a foreign key to Reader_Category. The fifth table, Borrowing_Information, has seven columns: Book_ID, Borrow_Date, Fine, Reader_ID, Renewal_Count, Return_Date, and a composite primary key consisting of Book_ID, Reader_ID, and Borrow_Date. Book_ID and Reader_ID are foreign keys to Book and Reader, respectively.",
  "gold_question": "The library management system is as follows:\nThe library has multiple books, each book has a Book ID, Title, Author, Publisher, Publication Date, Price, Book Type, and Content Description.     \nBook Type information is stored in the Book Category table, which includes Book Type ID, Type Name, and Description.\nThe library has multiple readers, each reader has a Reader ID, Reader Type, Contact Number, Credit Score, and Description.\nReader Type information is stored in the Reader Category table, which includes Reader Type ID, Type Name, and Description.\nThe borrowing process is recorded in the Borrowing table, each borrowing record has a Book ID, Reader ID, Borrow Date, Return Date, Renewal Count, and Fine.\nThe system manages book borrowing and returning, as well as reader borrowing permissions and credit scores through this information.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0133.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0133\nCREATE TABLE `book_category` (\n  `book_type_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `description` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `type_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`book_type_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `reader_category` (\n  `reader_type_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `description` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `type_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`reader_type_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `book` (\n  `book_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `author` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `book_type_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `content_description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `price` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `publication_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `publisher` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`book_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `book_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`book_type_id`) REFERENCES `book_category` (`book_type_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `reader` (\n  `reader_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `contact_number` varchar(20) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `credit_score` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `description` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `reader_type_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`reader_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `reader_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`reader_type_id`) REFERENCES `reader_category` (`reader_type_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `borrowing_information` (\n  `book_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `reader_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `borrow_date` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `fine` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `renewal_count` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `return_date` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`book_id`, `reader_id`, `borrow_date`),\n  CONSTRAINT `borrowing_information_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`book_id`) REFERENCES `book` (`book_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `borrowing_information_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`reader_id`) REFERENCES `reader` (`reader_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
